\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Macroscopic compatibility provides an objective comparison. The center panel shows that $\langle \boldsymbol  {\mathcal  F}_{12}\rangle $ follows the imposed shear, while $\langle (\mathbf  T_{\mathrm  {total}})_{12}\rangle $ turns away after intensive reconnecting. The right panel shows the same result in the Poincar\'e disk: the trajectory of the mean $\boldsymbol  {\mathcal  F}$ remains on the required pure-shear path, whereas the mean $\mathbf  T_{\mathrm  {total}}$ leaves it.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:compatibility}{{1}{2}{Macroscopic compatibility provides an objective comparison. The center panel shows that $\langle \Fm _{12}\rangle $ follows the imposed shear, while $\langle (\Ttotal )_{12}\rangle $ turns away after intensive reconnecting. The right panel shows the same result in the Poincar\'e disk: the trajectory of the mean $\Fm $ remains on the required pure-shear path, whereas the mean $\Ttotal $ leaves it}{figure.1}{}}
